<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Paranagua port operating normally.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Paranagua port operating normally.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Paranagua port was operating without problems on Thursday, a port official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're working full blast. Everything is functioning normally,&quot; Inspector Francisco Fanini, the port's chief of security, told Reuters.</p>
<p>A rumor circulated in Chicago grain markets Thursday that the port, a gateway for soybean exports, was closed.</p>
<p>On Thursday, nine vessels were in port including two unloading fertilizer, three container ships and at least one grain ship, Fanini said.</p>
<p>Brazil's annual carnival celebration starts on Friday evening and runs through Wednesday at midday. But Fanini said he had not heard of any plans for closure or repairs.</p>
<p>(Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5410)</p>
